---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const eula = 'https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/';
---

<Layout
  title="Support · Waycar"
  description="Get help with Waycar, the iPhone and iPad agent console: contact support, set up a Host, and fix common connection problems."
>
  <article class="section support">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="glass prose">
        <h1>Waycar Support</h1>
        <p>
          Waycar is an iPhone and iPad app for herdr and tmux. It connects to computers you control, called Hosts, over
          SSH or mosh, and shows the Agents running there. Waycar is made by OTREVA, LLC.
        </p>
        <p>
          For how each feature works, step by step, see <a href="/help"><strong>Waycar Help</strong></a>: one page per
          feature, with fixes for common problems.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@waycar.dev"><strong>support@waycar.dev</strong></a>. We answer every message by email.</p>
        <p>
          For discussion, bugs, and feature requests, join the community at
          <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/waycar/"><strong>r/waycar</strong></a> on Reddit. Both are also in the app under
          Settings › Support.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please tell us your iPhone or iPad model, its iOS version, the Waycar version (Settings › About), and what you
          see on screen. Never send passwords, private keys, tokens, or other secrets.
        </p>
        <p>For privacy questions or data requests, email <a href="mailto:privacy@waycar.dev"><strong>privacy@waycar.dev</strong></a>.</p>

        <h2>What you need</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>An iPhone or iPad with iOS or iPadOS 18 or later. An Android app is coming next.</li>
          <li>
            A Mac or Linux computer you control (a Host) running herdr 0.7.5 or later, or tmux 3.2 or later. See <a href="https://herdr.dev">herdr.dev</a>.
          </li>
          <li>SSH access to that Host. On a Mac, turn on Remote Login in System Settings › General › Sharing.</li>
          <li>Optional: Waycar's tools (the install command below), for Scan to Pair, Agent Notifications, Live Activities, Chat Mode, and status hooks.</li>
          <li>Optional: mosh-server on the Host, for connections that survive network changes.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Set up</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Install herdr on your Host and start it, or have tmux 3.2 or later on the Host.</li>
          <li>Add the Host to Waycar in one of two ways.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Scan to Pair (uses Waycar's tools)</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>
            On the Host, run: <code>curl -fsSL https://waycar.dev/install.sh | sh</code><br />
            The same command works for herdr, tmux, or both. It needs curl and tar, and no Node.js. It does not use sudo.
          </li>
          <li>
            Answer <strong>Y</strong> when it offers to show a Pairing Code. On herdr it pops up inside herdr. On tmux
            it draws in your terminal. Press <strong>c</strong> if you want to copy the code instead. On a Mac Host
            that copies it. On a Linux Host it shows the code so you can select it. The code expires in about 2 minutes.
          </li>
          <li>
            In Waycar, tap <strong>Scan to Pair</strong> and scan the code, or tap <strong>Paste Pairing Code</strong>.
            The Pairing Code carries the Host's local network addresses, so keep your device on the same network while
            you pair.
          </li>
          <li>Run the command again whenever you want to pair another device.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Add Manually (no install needed)</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>In Waycar, tap <strong>Add Manually</strong> on the welcome screen, or <strong>+</strong> (Add Host) in the Hosts list.</li>
          <li>
            Enter the Host's <strong>Address</strong> (a DNS name such as <code>mac.example.com</code> works best),
            <strong>Port</strong> (usually 22), and <strong>User</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Under <strong>Authentication</strong>, choose a <strong>Method</strong>:
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Password</strong>: type your login password for that user.</li>
              <li><strong>Device Key</strong>: copy the line Waycar shows and add it to <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> on the Host.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            Tap <strong>Save</strong>. When Waycar asks <strong>Trust this Host?</strong>, check the fingerprint (see
            "Host key" below) and tap <strong>Trust</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>Waycar runs its checks. When they pass, your Agents appear in the Console.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Common problems</h2>

        <h3>Host key: "Trust this Host?", "The host key is not trusted", or "The host key changed"</h3>
        <p>
          Waycar pins each Host's SSH host key the first time you connect. To check the fingerprint Waycar shows, run
          this on the Host; one of the SHA256 values it prints must match:
        </p>
        <p><code>for f in /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key.pub; do ssh-keygen -lf "$f"; done</code></p>
        <p>
          If you see "The host key is not trusted", open the Host's page and answer Trust this Host?. If you see "The
          host key changed" and you did not reinstall or replace the Host, do not trust the new key: someone may be
          intercepting the connection. If you did, open the Host's page and choose Trust New Key.
        </p>

        <h3>"herdr is not running on this Host"</h3>
        <p>
          Start herdr on the Host. If it is running, check that SSH stream-local forwarding is allowed: Waycar talks to
          herdr through its socket over SSH. In <code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</code>, <code>AllowStreamLocalForwarding</code>
          must not be <code>no</code> and <code>DisableForwarding</code> must not be <code>yes</code>. The line in
          <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> must not contain <code>restrict</code> or <code>no-port-forwarding</code>.
          Restart SSH on the Host after a change.
        </p>

        <h3>"herdr is not on this Host's SSH PATH"</h3>
        <p>
          SSH commands do not load your full shell profile. Homebrew installs herdr in <code>/opt/homebrew/bin</code>
          (Apple silicon Mac) or <code>/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin</code> (Linux). Make sure that folder is on the
          PATH for non-interactive SSH sessions.
        </p>

        <h3>"tmux is not installed on this Host"</h3>
        <p>
          Install tmux 3.2 or later, or herdr, on the Host.
        </p>

        <h3>"tmux is too old"</h3>
        <p>
          Waycar needs tmux 3.2 or later. Update tmux on the Host. If the Host also runs herdr, the install command
          ignores an old tmux and sets up herdr. Without herdr, it stops and tells you tmux is too old.
        </p>

        <h3>tmux Isn't Running on your Host</h3>
        <p>
          tmux has no sessions yet. Tap <strong>Start Session</strong> in the Console to start one, or start one on the
          Host.
        </p>

        <h3>Agents show Unknown on tmux</h3>
        <p>
          Waycar's status hooks tell it when an Agent is Working, Blocked, or Done. Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI,
          opencode and the other agents in <a href="/help/tmux-hooks">Waycar hooks for tmux</a> get hooks, but only if
          they were installed before you ran the install command. Run it again if you added one later. On the Host's
          page, <strong>Install Status Hooks</strong> does the same. Codex also needs a one-time review on its /hooks
          screen. Other Agents show Unknown.
        </p>

        <h3>One backend shows an issue on a Host with herdr and tmux</h3>
        <p>
          A Host can run both. If herdr or tmux fails, Waycar shows that issue with a <strong>Retry</strong> button while
          the other keeps working. To hide the tmux sessions on that Host, turn off <strong>Show tmux sessions</strong> on
          the Host's page. That also stops their notifications.
        </p>

        <h3>"Authentication failed"</h3>
        <p>
          Password sign-in uses SSH password authentication. If the Host only allows keys or keyboard-interactive
          sign-in, choose Device Key and add its line to <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code>.
        </p>

        <h3>Mosh does not connect</h3>
        <p>
          Mosh is optional. When it fails, Waycar uses SSH instead. To use mosh, install mosh-server on the Host
          (<code>brew install mosh</code> or <code>sudo apt install mosh</code>) and allow incoming UDP ports 60000 to
          61000 through the Host's firewall and router. Then edit the Host and tap <strong>Test Mosh on this Host</strong>.
        </p>

        <h3>IPv6-only networks</h3>
        <p>
          Some cellular and guest networks offer only IPv6. Waycar works there with a DNS name or an IP address; type
          IPv6 addresses without square brackets.
        </p>

        <h3>Pairing Code: "The Host has no pairing in progress for this code"</h3>
        <p>
          The code expired or was already used. Run the install command again, or show a new Pairing Code in herdr. On
          tmux, run the pair command the install command printed. Then scan the new code.
        </p>

        <h3>My computer is not reachable from the internet</h3>
        <p>
          Add a Jump Host: a server that you can reach and that can reach your computer. Enter it in the Host's Jump Host
          section. Waycar checks host keys at both hops.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Your SSH keys, passwords, commands, and terminal output go only between your device and your Hosts. If you turn
          on AI Summaries, your Host also sends recent screen text to its AI provider.
          <a href="/privacy">Read the full privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Company</h2>
        <p>
          Waycar is an independent app from OTREVA, LLC. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the herdr project,
          CodexBar, Anthropic, OpenAI or Google.
        </p>
        <p>Waycar is licensed under <a href={eula}>Apple's standard end user license agreement</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 80ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.4vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 620;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 32px;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  p,
  ul,
  ol {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  li ul {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  ul,
  ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: disc;
  }

  ol {
    list-style: decimal;
  }

  li::marker {
    color: var(--violet-soft);
  }

  strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--cyan);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  code {
    padding: 1px 6px;
    font-size: 0.88em;
    color: var(--text);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    background: rgb(var(--white-rgb) / 0.06);
    border-radius: var(--radius-code);
  }
</style>
